---
import StaticPage from '../layouts/StaticPage.astro';
import { SITE_NAME } from '../consts';
---

<StaticPage
  title="Terms"
  description={`Terms of use for ${SITE_NAME}.`}
  canonicalPath="/terms/"
  updated="September 2026"
>
  <p>
    These Terms govern your use of {SITE_NAME} (the "Site"). By accessing the Site,
    you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the Site.
  </p>

  <h2>Use of content</h2>
  <p>
    Editorial content on this Site is made available for your personal,
    non-commercial reading. You may share links and brief excerpts with attribution.
    Republishing full articles, in whole or in part, requires prior written
    permission.
  </p>

  <h2>Automated and AI-assisted content</h2>
  <p>
    Some content may be produced or assisted by automated systems. Such content is
    labeled accordingly and is subject to editorial review before publication.
  </p>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Do not attempt to disrupt or compromise the Site or its servers.</li>
    <li>Do not scrape content at scale without permission.</li>
    <li>Do not misrepresent your affiliation with the Site.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Third-party links</h2>
  <p>
    The Site may link to third-party websites. We are not responsible for the
    content or practices of those sites.
  </p>

  <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
  <p>
    Content is provided "as is" without warranties of any kind. While our articles
    are derived from official government sources, we are an independent
    publication and are not affiliated with those agencies. Always refer to the
    linked official source for the most current information.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent permitted by law, {SITE_NAME} is not liable for any
    indirect or consequential damages arising from your use of the Site.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may revise these Terms from time to time. Continued use after changes
    constitutes acceptance of the revised Terms.
  </p>
</StaticPage>
